From: OpenHarmony PC porting (libomptarget-rtl-amdgpu 18.1.8)
Subject: [PATCH] ompt: consult the global namespace for the application tool on OHOS

OMPT tools embedded in the application are found through the weak ompt_start_tool
symbol in libomp: the tool's strong definition in the main executable is expected
to preempt the runtime's weak definition when the loader binds the internal call.
glibc does this, but the OHOS (musl) loader does not preempt a versioned weak
definition in a DSO with an unversioned strong definition from the executable
(libomp exports its symbols with a VERSION script), so the weak definition
survives the bind and its dlsym(RTLD_NEXT) lookup can never see symbols defined
by the executable, which precedes libomp in the search order. Net effect: an
application-embedded OMPT tool is silently ignored on OHOS and its ompt_get_*
inquiries return NULL (which then crashes the ompt test suite at the first
dereference).

On __OHOS__, consult the global namespace explicitly with dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT,
"ompt_start_tool") before falling back to the RTLD_NEXT chain, skipping libomp's
own definition to avoid recursion. Behavior is unchanged on other platforms.

diff --git a/openmp/runtime/src/ompt-general.cpp b/openmp/runtime/src/ompt-general.cpp
index 95aab6c..3ebdb89 100644
--- a/openmp/runtime/src/ompt-general.cpp
+++ b/openmp/runtime/src/ompt-general.cpp
@@ -160,6 +160,22 @@ static ompt_start_tool_result_t *ompt_tool_darwin(unsigned int omp_version,
 _OMP_EXTERN OMPT_WEAK_ATTRIBUTE ompt_start_tool_result_t *
 ompt_start_tool(unsigned int omp_version, const char *runtime_version) {
   ompt_start_tool_result_t *ret = NULL;
+#if defined(__OHOS__)
+  // The OHOS (musl) dynamic loader does not preempt libomp's versioned
+  // weak ompt_start_tool with an unversioned strong definition from the
+  // application, so the tool embedded in the executable would never be
+  // found through the bind. Look it up in the global namespace explicitly;
+  // skip libomp's own (weak) definition to avoid resolving to ourselves.
+  ompt_start_tool_t app_tool =
+      (ompt_start_tool_t)dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, "ompt_start_tool");
+  if (app_tool &&
+      app_tool != (ompt_start_tool_t)&ompt_start_tool) {
+    ret = app_tool(omp_version, runtime_version);
+    if (ret) {
+      return ret;
+    }
+  }
+#endif
   // Search next symbol in the current address space. This can happen if the
   // runtime library is linked before the tool. Since glibc 2.2 strong symbols
   // don't override weak symbols that have been found before unless the user
